<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  The landing blast's armor penetration on Combat Extended's scale. CE leaves a third party's
  GenExplosion.DoExplosion alone, so the blast, the roof punch and the structure damage run as
  in vanilla; what changes is the armor math its injuries go through, where penetration is
  compared with blunt armor in megapascals and a blunt hit that does not exceed the rating is
  deflected to zero. The main tree's 0.15 reads as 0.15 MPa there, under any CE shirt, so an
  unpatched landing hurts nobody who is dressed. 6 is CE's own rule for an explosion of 20
  damage (penetration 0.3 x damage; its 40 mm HE grenade lands at about 6.6, a frag grenade
  at about 17), which keeps the blast's vanilla place: it wounds the unarmored and the
  flak-vested (CE 12) and bounces off power armor. The extension's field is the one the
  ability passes; the DamageDef's default is moved with it so the two stay the same number.
  The settings' penetration row stores this unit under its own key while CE is active
  (Source/1.6/Settings/Settings_Landing.cs).
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/VEF.Abilities.AbilityDef[defName="SCWC_BreachJump"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="ShipcrackerWarcasket.BreachJumpExtension"]/breachArmorPenetration</xpath>
    <value>
      <breachArmorPenetration>6</breachArmorPenetration>
    </value>
  </Operation>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/DamageDef[defName="SCWC_Breach"]/defaultArmorPenetration</xpath>
    <value>
      <defaultArmorPenetration>6</defaultArmorPenetration>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
